# Section Composer — Multi-Achievement Bullet Generation

Add a "Section Composer" mode to the Bullet Laboratory that lets users generate optimized resume bullet sets from an entire heading/group of achievements, with AI-driven merging, prioritization, and exclusion reasoning.

## How It Works (User Flow)

```mermaid
graph TD
    A["User opens Lab"] --> B{"Select Mode"}
    B -->|"Single Achievement"| C["Existing flow unchanged"]
    B -->|"Section Composer"| D["Select Parent Heading<br/>(e.g. Accenture Song)"]
    D --> E["Select Domain + # of Points"]
    E --> F{"Achievement Selection"}
    F -->|"All (default)"| G["AI sees all achievements<br/>under that heading"]
    F -->|"Custom Select"| H["User checkmarks<br/>specific achievements"]
    G --> I["Optional: Benchmark text"]
    H --> I
    I --> J["Generate"]
    J --> K["AI Output: N optimized bullets<br/>+ exclusion reasoning<br/>+ merge explanations"]
    K --> L["Resume-style preview"]
    L --> M["Save individually or as batch"]
```

### Key UX Details
- The Lab tab keeps both modes: a **toggle** at the top switches between "Single Achievement" and "Section Composer"
- Section Composer groups headings exactly like the Vault does (by `parent_experience`)
- When a heading is selected, all its achievements appear as checkboxes (all checked by default)
- User specifies number of points (slider or number input, 2–6 range)
- The output renders in a **resume-section preview** layout (heading + timeline + bullets)

